WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:08.100
We are given the task of planning a new city.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:10.820
What would the list of necessities include?

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:14.480
A medical care center, market area, garden,

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:17.620
shopping center, educational institutes

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:19.720
and so many in the list !

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:22.700
Apart from these, the proper supply of water

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:24.840
and a well designed sewerage system

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:27.720
tops the chart of requirements !

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:30.100
are we missing something important ?

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:33.580
For every house to be functioning properly,

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:36.000
don’t we need a power supply ?

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:37.500
Of course yes !

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:40.500
Power supply is one of the most essential requirements

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:42.460
of every home today.

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:44.760
Without it, functioning of important

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:47.700
and useful gadgets is not possible !

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:49.860
Similarly, in our cells,

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:51.420
for the organelles to work,

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:54.860
there has to be a continuous supply of energy.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:56.220
So which organelle

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:59.740
takes the responsibility of supplying this energy ?

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:02.060
It’s the mitochondria.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:05.020
The double membrane organelle is called as

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:08.420
power house of the cell because it produces molecules

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.020
which are the usable form of energy for the cell.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:14.420
What do we mean by usable form of energy

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:16.180
in the first place ?

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:19.740
Well, let’s say we want to buy something from a shop.

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:21.580
What will we give the shopkeeper

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:23.320
in return of the goods ?

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:26.000
Can we just give him pieces of paper ?

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:27.460
Of course not !

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:29.140
We give proper currency notes

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:31.780
and not just pieces of paper.

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:34.900
That is because although both are made up of paper,

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:37.800
currency notes are the standardized forms with

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:39.600
immense value.

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:42.040
So we can say that these currency notes

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:45.200
are the usable forms.

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:47.900
If the same sized piece of paper is given,

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.200
then that will not be considered as a currency.

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:54.360
Because the usable form is the actual standard

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.900
and accepted currency note!

00:01:57.020 --> 00:02:00.760
Similarly, the food we eat gives us energy.

00:02:00.860 --> 00:02:01.920
We know this.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:05.620
But the energy from the food is not in the usable form.

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:08.640
So the enzymes in the mitochondria convert

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:11.360
these energy molecules into usable molecules

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:14.520
called the Adenosine triphosphate .

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:17.500
It is abbreviated as ATP .

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:21.640
So are these ATP molecules the usable forms ?

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:22.700
That's Right.

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:25.900
Cells can obtain energy when these ATP molecules

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:27.620
are broken down.

00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:31.200
So how does this power house of the cell look like ?

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:33.880
The mitochondria , has two membranes

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:37.080
the outer membrane and the inner membrane.

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:39.520
The outer membrane is PORUOS which means

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:43.380
it allows the TRANSPORT of materials across itself.

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:45.640
The inner membrane is slightly different

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:47.520
and interesting to understand.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:50.440
The membrane is thrown into several folds

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:53.860
and therefore has a LARGER surface area.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:56.920
These folds are referred to as “Cristae”.

00:02:57.040 --> 00:03:00.360
But what is the use of a larger surface area?

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:03.380
A larger surface area would be a wider base

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:06.940
for ATP generating chemical reactions.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:08.560
Because the larger area

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:12.600
will harbor more enzymes that will produce ATP .

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:15.720
The inner part of this membrane has a matrix which

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:19.980
contains all the necessary enzymes for ATP production.

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:22.500
Thus, larger the surface area,

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:26.720
larger will be the amount of ATP molecules generated !

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:30.120
Apart from this, the organelle has its own DNA

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:33.160
and ribosomes just like the NUCLEUS.

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:36.760
Therefore mitochondria can make its own proteins

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:39.140
and replicate on its own.

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:41.160
That means make its copies

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:44.380
independent of the other organelles.

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:47.140
Now that we have got introduced to this extremely

00:03:47.180 --> 00:03:49.800
important organelle, let us have a look at

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:52.660
one more interesting organelle in the list.

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:56.480
Let us have a look at “VACUOLES ” in the next video!

